INT. COURTHOUSE BASEMENT - EVIDENCE CAGE - DAY

A wire-mesh room under flickering fluorescents. Shelves of banker's boxes, tagged in marker. A steel table in the middle. The ceiling pipes drip.

ATTORNEY COLETTE BAPTISTE (40s, pinstripe suit, rolling briefcase) sets a box on the table. CLERK ARNOLD (60s, cardigan, coin purse of keys) stands at the cage door, a sign-in book open on a stand. GUARD TREVOR (30s, county uniform, a thermos) leans on the wall, unhurried.

COLETTE
Mr. Arnold, I'd like to inspect Exhibit Fourteen.

ARNOLD
You'll need to sign the book.

COLETTE
I've signed it.

ARNOLD
Not the second page.

COLETTE
There's a second page?

ARNOLD
Since March.

She signs. Arnold inspects the signature, sniffs, and nods. Colette opens the box. She lifts out a plastic bag with a worn leather wallet.

COLETTE (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Come on, come on.

She slides the wallet out, checks its contents, frowns.

TREVOR
Anything wrong, counselor?

COLETTE
(to Trevor)
No. Just a count.

TREVOR
We count everything twice down here.

COLETTE
That's reassuring.

She peers at the bag's seal. The tape is peeled at one corner and re-pressed.

COLETTE (CONT'D)
Mr. Arnold. When was this box last opened?

ARNOLD
It's in the log.

COLETTE
I'd like you to read the log aloud.

ARNOLD
That's not standard.

COLETTE
It's a request.

Arnold sighs, flips pages, finds a line, runs his finger along it.

ARNOLD
October third. Detective Sahar Qureshi, from Major Crimes.

COLETTE
Not mine.

ARNOLD
She said it was for a review.

TREVOR
She wasn't on the list.

ARNOLD
(to Trevor)
She had a badge.

TREVOR
Badges aren't lists, Arnold.

The door at the end of the corridor buzzes. A heavy tread. INVESTIGATOR SAHAR QURESHI (40s, trench coat, short hair, a folder under her arm) enters the cage, nods to the room.

SAHAR
Morning, all. I hear someone's asking about me.

COLETTE
Detective Qureshi.

SAHAR
Counselor. How's the Delacroix case?

COLETTE
Not the topic. You opened my exhibit.

SAHAR
I opened a lot of exhibits.

COLETTE
You re-taped the seal.

SAHAR
Did I? I'd have to check.

Colette crosses her arms. Trevor takes a long, noisy sip from his thermos. Arnold scribbles in his log.

ARNOLD
(muttering, to himself)
Second page, second page.

SAHAR
I'd be careful what you write, Arnold.

ARNOLD
I write what's true.

COLETTE
(to Sahar)
I'll need an affidavit explaining why you accessed Exhibit Fourteen on October third.

SAHAR
I'd be glad to.

COLETTE
Today.

SAHAR
It's Tuesday. Courts close at four.

COLETTE
Then you'll have to be fast.

Sahar smiles faintly. She sets her folder on the table and flips it open. Inside, a thick packet of photographs.

SAHAR
Or I could show you what I found.

Colette stares at the photographs. Her face doesn't change, but her hand drifts to the table edge.

COLETTE
Where did you get those?

SAHAR
Inside the wallet's lining.

TREVOR
(to himself)
Told you we count twice.

ARNOLD
(to the room)
Everyone please remember to initial the second page on your way out.

COLETTE
Detective.

SAHAR
Counselor.

COLETTE
(flat)
Let's go upstairs.

^SAHAR
(flat)
Let's go upstairs.

Colette takes the box. Sahar takes the folder. They walk out side by side. Trevor and Arnold exchange a look.

TREVOR
That's going to be a long Tuesday.

ARNOLD
They're always long. That's why we sign.
